        <main class="content">
          
<div class="page-header">
  <div>
    <a class="back-link" href="/collection/1"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg> fixture</a>
    <h1>What changed</h1>
    
    
    <div class="page-header__sub">
      
      Files in <strong>fixture</strong> that went missing or changed. Recover anything you want
      back, then clear the alerts — <strong>Mark reviewed</strong> to just note them, or use the
      action below that names what you want done. Each acts only on the files it names.
    </div>
    
  </div>
  
  <div class="page-header__actions">
    <span id="review-open-pill">
  <span class="pill pill--soft pill--danger pill--sm">2 unreviewed</span>
</span>
  </div>
</div>




  
  <div class="card recovery" id="recovery"
       data-root="<TMP>/fixture"
       data-relpaths="gone/delta.txt
mod/gamma.txt">
    <div class="recovery__head">
      <div class="recovery__title"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 4v12M7 11l5 5 5-5"/><path d="M5 20h14"/></svg> Recover these files</div>
      <div class="recovery__actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm" data-copy="rel"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h8"/></svg> Copy paths</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn--sm" data-copy="abs"><svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="9" y="9" width="11" height="11" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h8"/></svg> Copy full paths</button>
        <span class="recovery__copied" id="recovery-copied" hidden>Copied ✓</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="recovery__hint">
      Cairn watches your files read-only — it never restores them itself. Paste the copied list into
      your own backup tool (restic, Borg, rsync, Time Machine, a cloud sync…) to bring them back, then
      <strong>Scan now</strong> on the collection to check what you restored: each returned file is
      re-read and compared against the fingerprint Cairn recorded before it went missing. Files that
      match are cleared; a file whose contents differ — the wrong snapshot, a truncated restore —
      closes the now-obsolete <em>missing</em> alert and replaces it with a new
      <em>came back changed</em> alert. Or
      <strong>Stop tracking</strong> the files that are gone for good.
      
      
    </div>
    <details class="recovery__more">
      <summary>How to recover (any backup tool)</summary>
      <ol class="recovery__steps">
        <li>Copy the affected paths with the <strong>Copy paths</strong> button above (relative to the collection root, or full paths).</li>
        <li>In your backup tool, restore exactly those paths to the collection root <span class="mono"><TMP>/fixture</span>.</li>
        <li>Run <strong>Scan now</strong> on the collection page. Every file that reappeared is re-read
          and compared against the fingerprint recorded before it went missing: a file whose contents
          match flips back to <em>restored / OK</em>; a file whose contents differ is flagged
          <em>came back changed</em>, which closes the obsolete <em>missing</em> alert and raises a
          new one in its place — check that one before you trust it.</li>
        <li>For anything you don't want back, <strong>Stop tracking</strong> it — from the button above, or one file at a time from its row.</li>
      </ol>
    </details>
  </div>

  
  <div class="card resolve">
    <div class="resolve__head"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.9" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8.5 12l2.5 2.5 4.5-5"/></svg> Clear these alerts</div>
    <div class="resolve__sub">Two ways to resolve, depending on whether the change was expected.</div>
    <div class="resolve__grid">
      <div class="resolve__opt">
        <div class="resolve__opt-head">
          <span class="resolve__chip resolve__chip--ack"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg></span>
          <div>
            <div class="resolve__opt-title">Mark reviewed</div>
            <span class="pill pill--soft pill--muted pill--sm">Baseline unchanged</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="resolve__opt-desc">
          You've reviewed these. Cairn keeps watching and keeps your baseline — each file stays on
          record as missing or changed and any existence proof is kept. Clears the alert, but it can
          return if the file changes again.
        </div>
        
          <form method="post" action="/collection/1/review/ack-all">
    <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<CSRF>" />
    <button class="btn btn--subtle btn--full" type="submit"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg> Mark all 2 reviewed</button>
    <div class="field__hint">Clears 2 alerts in this collection. Nothing about the files changes.</div>
  </form>
        
      </div>
      
      <div class="resolve__opt resolve__opt--accept">
        <div class="resolve__opt-head">
          <span class="resolve__chip resolve__chip--accept"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-3-6.7L21 8"/><path d="M21 4v4h-4"/></svg></span>
          <div>
            <div class="resolve__opt-title">Accept as new baseline</div>
            <span class="pill pill--soft pill--warn pill--sm">Rewrites your baseline</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="resolve__opt-desc">
          Treat the current state as correct from now on. Each action below touches only the files
          it names — nothing else in this collection changes, and nothing on disk is deleted. Use
          these when <em>you</em> made the change.
        </div>
        
          <form method="post" action="/collection/1/review/adopt-changed" class="resolve__verb"
                onsubmit="return confirm('Adopt 1 changed file? Their current contents become the expected version, and this change will not be reported again.');">
            <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<CSRF>" />
            
            <input type="hidden" name="population_fp" value="608b257f6ed91dc6d0ec25adca50e19811020186160ea0c403e410a4f588144e" />
            <button class="btn btn--subtle btn--full" type="submit"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-3-6.7L21 8"/><path d="M21 4v4h-4"/></svg> Adopt 1 changed file</button>
            <div class="field__hint">Treats the current contents as correct from now on. Cairn recorded and notarized the new contents when it detected the change; this stops the alert. You won't be told about this change again.</div>
          </form>
        
        
          <form method="post" action="/collection/1/review/stop-tracking" class="resolve__verb"
                onsubmit="return confirm('Stop tracking 1 missing file? Their records are permanently removed from Cairn — paths, first-seen dates, and the link to their timestamp proofs. Nothing on disk is deleted and the .ots proof files stay in the proof store.');">
            <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<CSRF>" />
            <input type="hidden" name="population_fp" value="48f156c4dc99923c8da105110cc862e9361d87d4e307c8ae3b26e8769925f2a1" />
            
            <button class="btn btn--danger btn--full" type="submit"><svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12h8"/></svg> Stop tracking 1 missing file</button>
            <div class="field__hint">Permanently removes 1 file from Cairn's records — their paths, first-seen dates, and the link to their timestamp proofs. Nothing on disk is deleted and the .ots proof files stay in the proof store, but Cairn will no longer list them under Verify. If you want them back, restore from backup and run a scan instead.</div>
          </form>
        
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card card--flush review-list">
    <div class="review-list__head">
      <h3>2 files to review</h3>
      <div class="review-list__legend">
        <span class="legend__stat"><span class="dot"><span class="dot__core" style="width:7px;height:7px;background:var(--danger)"></span>
</span>1 missing</span>
        <span class="legend__stat"><span class="dot"><span class="dot__core" style="width:7px;height:7px;background:var(--warn)"></span>
</span>1 modified</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="field__hint" style="padding:0 18px 12px;margin-top:0">
      <strong>Mark reviewed:</strong> Notes that you've seen this. The file stays on record as missing or changed, keeps any existence proof, and the collection keeps its Alert status until you restore or retire it.
    </div>
    
      



<div class="review-row" id="review-row-4">
  <div class="review-row__icon review-row__icon--danger">
    <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12h8"/></svg>
  </div>
  <div class="review-row__body">
    
    <div class="review-row__path" title="gone/delta.txt">
      <span class="review-row__dir mono">gone/</span>
      <span class="review-row__name mono">delta.txt</span>
    </div>
    <div class="review-row__story">
      
        Gone from disk — last seen <AGO> <span class="review-row__when">(<DATETIME> UTC)</span>
      
      <span class="review-row__sep">·</span> 10 B
      
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="review-row__action">
    
    
      <form method="post" action="/collection/1/file/4/accept" style="display:inline"
            data-relpath="gone/delta.txt"
            onsubmit="return confirm('Stop tracking ' + this.dataset.relpath + '? Its record is permanently removed from Cairn — path, first-seen date, and the link to its timestamp proof. Nothing on disk is deleted and the .ots proof file stays in the proof store.');">
        <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<CSRF>" />
        <input type="hidden" name="population_fp" value="0c4d73b793ccdc4d1d1567a6c14d21490a0778308123164f57c802d5ac2b1a1b" />
        
          <button class="btn btn--sm btn--danger" type="submit"
                  title="Permanently removes this file from Cairn's records — its path, first-seen date, and the link to its timestamp proof. Nothing on disk is deleted and the .ots proof file stays in the proof store.">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M8 12h8"/></svg> Stop tracking this file
          </button>
        
      </form>
    
    
      <span class="pill pill--soft pill--muted pill--sm"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg> Reviewed</span>
    
  </div>
</div>
    
      



<div class="review-row" id="review-row-3">
  <div class="review-row__icon review-row__icon--warn">
    <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M10.3 3.8 2.4 18a1.9 1.9 0 0 0 1.7 2.9h15.8a1.9 1.9 0 0 0 1.7-2.9L13.7 3.8a1.9 1.9 0 0 0-3.4 0z"/><path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01"/></svg>
  </div>
  <div class="review-row__body">
    
    <div class="review-row__path" title="mod/gamma.txt">
      <span class="review-row__dir mono">mod/</span>
      <span class="review-row__name mono">gamma.txt</span>
    </div>
    <div class="review-row__story">
      
        Contents changed — detected never
      
      <span class="review-row__sep">·</span> 10 B
      
        <span class="review-row__proof" title="An OpenTimestamps proof attests this file existed before it was lost — it survives even though the bytes are gone."><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M9.5 7.5h4a2.2 2.2 0 0 1 0 4.5h-4M9.5 12h4.3a2.2 2.2 0 0 1 0 4.5H9.5M9.5 7.5v9M11 6v1.5M11 16.5V18M13 6v1.5M13 16.5V18"/></svg> proof of prior existence kept</span>
      
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="review-row__action">
    
    
      <form method="post" action="/collection/1/file/3/accept" style="display:inline"
            data-relpath="mod/gamma.txt"
            onsubmit="return confirm('Adopt the current contents of ' + this.dataset.relpath + ' as correct from now on? This change will not be reported again.');">
        <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="<CSRF>" />
        <input type="hidden" name="population_fp" value="e40b9d527852e835e7772d85dbb7059f06171628692e40583ef1a8051d9a7298" />
        
          <button class="btn btn--sm btn--warn-outline" type="submit"
                  title="Treats the current contents as correct from now on. Cairn recorded and notarized the new contents when it detected the change; this stops the alert. You won't be told about this change again.">
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-3-6.7L21 8"/><path d="M21 4v4h-4"/></svg> Adopt this change
          </button>
        
      </form>
    
    
      <span class="pill pill--soft pill--muted pill--sm"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg> Reviewed</span>
    
  </div>
</div>
    
    
  </div>


<script>
  (function () {
    var card = document.getElementById("recovery");
    if (!card) return;
    var rel = card.getAttribute("data-relpaths") || "";
    var root = card.getAttribute("data-root") || "";
    function paths(kind) {
      if (!rel) return "";
      if (kind === "rel") return rel;
      var base = root.replace(/\/+$/, "");
      return rel.split("\n").map(function (p) { return base + "/" + p; }).join("\n");
    }
    // The insecure-origin fallback and the visible "Copied ✓" / failure state live in
    // partials/_clipboard.html (window.cairnCopy), shared with the verify card so the two copy
    // surfaces cannot drift. A failed copy has to *say so*: silently doing nothing leaves the
    // operator pasting a stale clipboard into their backup tool and restoring the wrong paths.
    card.querySelectorAll("[data-copy]").forEach(function (btn) {
      btn.addEventListener("click", function () {
        window.cairnCopy(paths(btn.getAttribute("data-copy")), "recovery-copied");
      });
    });
  })();
</script>

        </main>
      </div>
    </div>
    
    
<script>
  (function () {
    // Hidden-textarea + execCommand: the pre-async-clipboard path, still the only one that works
    // on an insecure origin. Also the fallback when a secure-context write is rejected (permission
    // policy, a document that isn't focused).
    function legacyCopy(text) {
      try {
        var ta = document.createElement("textarea");
        ta.value = text;
        ta.setAttribute("readonly", "");
        ta.style.position = "fixed";
        ta.style.top = "-1000px";
        ta.style.opacity = "0";
        document.body.appendChild(ta);
        ta.select();
        ta.setSelectionRange(0, ta.value.length);
        var ok = document.execCommand("copy");
        document.body.removeChild(ta);
        return !!ok;
      } catch (e) {
        return false;
      }
    }

    // The visible outcome. `note` is an element or the id of one; a caller with nowhere to report
    // to still gets the copy attempted.
    window.cairnCopyReport = function (note, ok) {
      if (typeof note === "string") { note = document.getElementById(note); }
      if (!note) return;
      note.textContent = ok ? "Copied ✓" : "Couldn't copy — select the text and copy it manually";
      note.style.color = ok ? "" : "var(--danger)";
      note.hidden = false;
      setTimeout(function () { note.hidden = true; }, ok ? 1800 : 5000);
    };

    window.cairnCopy = function (text, note) {
      if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) {
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(function () {
          window.cairnCopyReport(note, true);
        }).catch(function () {
          window.cairnCopyReport(note, legacyCopy(text));
        });
      } else {
        window.cairnCopyReport(note, legacyCopy(text));
      }
    };
  })();
</script>
    <script>
      // Mobile nav drawer: the hamburger toggles `body.nav-open`; the backdrop and any sidebar
      // link close it. No-op on desktop (the drawer styles only apply under the breakpoint).
      (function () {
        var body = document.body;
        var close = function () { body.classList.remove("nav-open"); };
        var toggle = document.getElementById("nav-toggle");
        if (toggle) {
          toggle.addEventListener("click", function () { body.classList.toggle("nav-open"); });
        }
        var backdrop = document.getElementById("nav-backdrop");
        if (backdrop) { backdrop.addEventListener("click", close); }
        document.querySelectorAll(".sidebar a").forEach(function (a) {
          a.addEventListener("click", close);
        });
      })();
    </script>
  </body>
</html>